{
  "title": "37: al-Saaffaat الصافات",
  "code": "012",
  "data": "بِسْمِ اللهِ الرَّحْمٰنِ الرَّحِيْمِ\nBISMIL LAAHIR RAHMAANIR RAHEEM\nIn the Name of Allah, the All-merciful, the All-compassionate\nوَالصّٰٓفّٰتِ صَفًّا ۙ‏(1)\nWAALSSAAAFFAATE MALAAA-EKATO.\nBy those who range themselves in ranks, \nفَالزّٰجِرٰتِ زَجْرًا ۙ‏(2)\nFAALZZAAJERAATE ZAJRAN.\nAnd so are strong in repelling (evil), \nفَالتّٰلِيٰتِ ذِكْرًا ۙ‏(3)\nFAALTTAALEETE ZIKRAA.\nAnd thus proclaim the Message (of Allah)! \nاِنَّ اِلٰهَكُمْ لَوَاحِدٌ ؕ‏(4)\nINNAL AELAAHAKUM LAWAAHEDUN.\nVerily, verily, your Allah is one!- \nرَبُّ السَّمٰوٰتِ وَالْاَرْضِ وَمَا بَيْنَهُمَا وَرَبُّ الْمَشَارِقِ ؕ‏(5)\nRABBUL SAMAAWAATE WAL ARZE WA MAA BAYNAHOMAA WA RABBO AL-MASHAAREQE.\nLord of the heavens and of the earth and all between them, and Lord of every point at the rising of the sun! \nاِنَّا زَيَّنَّا السَّمَآءَ الدُّنْيَا بِزِيْنَةِ اۨلْكَوَاكِبِۙ‏(6)\nINNAA ZAYYANNAA SAMAAA-AD DUNYAA BEZEENATE AL-KAWAAKEBE.\nWe have indeed decked the lower heaven with beauty (in) the stars, \nوَحِفْظًا مِّنْ كُلِّ شَيْطٰنٍ مَّارِدٍۚ‏(7)\nWAHEFZAN MIN KULLE SHAYTAANIR MMAAREDIN.\n(For beauty) and for guard against all obstinate rebellious evil spirits, \nلَّا يَسَّمَّعُوْنَ اِلَى الْمَلَاِ الْاَعْلٰى وَيُقْذَفُوْنَ مِنْ كُلِّ جَانِبٍۖ ‏(8)\nLAA YASSAMMAU’OONA ELAL MALA-E A-A’LAA WAYUQZAFOONA MIN KULLE JAANEBIN.\n(So) they should not strain their ears in the direction of the Exalted Assembly but be cast away from every side, \nدُحُوْرًا  وَّلَهُمْ عَذَابٌ وَّاصِبٌ  ۙ‏(9)\nDUHOORAN WA LAHUM A’ZAABUN WWAASEBUN.\nRepulsed, for they are under a perpetual penalty, \nاِلَّا مَنْ خَطِفَ الْخَطْفَةَ فَاَتْبَعَهٗ شِهَابٌ ثَاقِبٌ‏(10)\nILLAA MAN KHATEFA AL-KHATFATA FAATBAA’AH SHEHAABUN SAAQEBUN.\nExcept such as snatch away something by stealth, and they are pursued by a flaming fire, of piercing brightness. \nفَاسْتَفْتِهِمْ اَهُمْ اَشَدُّ خَلْقًا اَمْ مَّنْ خَلَقْنَاؕ اِنَّا خَلَقْنٰهُمْ مِّنْ طِيْنٍ لَّازِبٍ‏(11)\nFAASTAFTEHEM A HUM ASHADDO KHALQAN AM MAN KHALAQNAA INNAA KHALAQNAAHUM MIN TEENIN LLAAZEBIN.\nJust ask their opinion: are they the more difficult to create, or the (other) beings We have created? Them have We created out of a sticky clay! \nبَلْ عَجِبْتَ وَيَسْخَرُوْنَ‏(12)\nBAL A’AJEBTA WA YASKHAROONA.\nTruly dost thou marvel, while they ridicule, \nوَاِذَا ذُكِّرُوْا لَا يَذْكُرُوْنَ‏(13)\nWA EZAA ZUKKEROOA LAA YAZKUROONA.\nAnd, when they are admonished, pay no heed, \nوَاِذَا رَاَوْا اٰيَةً يَّسْتَسْخِرُوْنَ‏(14)\nWA EZAA RA-AW AAYATAL YYASTASKHEROONA.\nAnd, when they see a Sign, turn it to mockery, \nوَقَالُوْۤا اِنْ هٰذَاۤ اِلَّا سِحْرٌ مُّبِيْنٌ ۖۚ‏(15)\nWA QAALOO IN HAAZAA ILLAA SEHRUM MOBEEN.\nAnd say, “This is nothing but evident sorcery! \nءَاِذَا مِتْنَا وَكُنَّا تُرَابًا وَّعِظَامًا ءَاِنَّا لَمَبْعُوْثُوْنَۙ‏(16)\nA-EZAA MITNAA KUNNAA TORAABANW WA E’ZAAMAN A-INNAA LA-MABO’OSOON.\n“What! when we die, and become dust and bones, shall we (then) be raised up (again) \nاَوَاٰبَآؤُنَا الْاَوَّلُوْنَؕ‏(17)\nAWA-AABAAA-ONAL AL-AAWLOONA.\n“And also our fathers of old?” \nقُلْ نَعَمْ وَاَنْتُمْ دٰخِرُوْنَۚ‏(18)\nQUL NAA’AM WA ANTUM DAAKHEROONA.\nSay thou: “Yea, and ye shall then be humiliated (on account of your evil).” \nفَاِنَّمَا هِىَ زَجْرَةٌ وَّاحِدَةٌ فَاِذَا هُمْ يَنْظُرُوْنَ‏(19)\nFA-INNAMAA HEYA ZAJRATUN WWAAHEDATUN FA-EZAA HUM YANZOROONA.\nThen it will be a single (compelling) cry; and behold, they will begin to see! \nوَقَالُوْا يٰوَيْلَنَا هٰذَا يَوْمُ الدِّيْنِ‏(20)\nWA QAALOO YAA WAYLANAA HAAZAA YAWMUD DEENE.\nThey will say, “Ah! Woe to us! This is the Day of Judgment!” \nهٰذَا يَوْمُ الْفَصْلِ الَّذِىْ كُنْتُمْ بِهٖ تُكَذِّبُوْنَ‏(21)\nHAAZAA YAWMUD FASLE LAZEE KUNTUM BEHI TOKAZZEBOON.\n(A voice will say,) “This is the Day of Sorting Out, whose truth ye (once) denied!” \nاُحْشُرُوا الَّذِيْنَ ظَلَمُوْا وَاَزْوَاجَهُمْ وَمَا كَانُوْا يَعْبُدُوْنَۙ‏(22)\nAUHSHUROOA LAZEENA ZALAMOO WAAZWAAJAHUM WA MAA KAANOO YA’BODOON.\n“Bring ye up”, it shall be said, “The wrong-doers and their wives, and the things they worshipped- \nمِنْ دُوْنِ اللّٰهِ فَاهْدُوْهُمْ اِلٰى صِرَاطِ الْجَحِيْمِ‏(23)\nMIN DOONIL LAAHE FAAHDOOHUM ELAA SERAATE JAHEEM.\n“Besides Allah, and lead them to the Way to the (Fierce) Fire! \nوَقِفُوْهُمْ اِنَّهُمْ مَّسْئُوْلُوْنَۙ‏(24)\nWAQEFOOHUM INNAHUM MMASOOLOONA.\n“But stop them, for they must be asked: \nمَا لَكُمْ لَا تَنَاصَرُوْنَ‏(25)\nMAA LAKUM LAA TANAASAROONA.\n“'What is the matter with you that ye help not each other?'“ \nبَلْ هُمُ الْيَوْمَ مُسْتَسْلِمُوْنَ‏(26)\nBAL HOMUL YAWMA MUSTASLEMOONA.\nNay, but that day they shall submit (to Judgment); \nوَاَقْبَلَ بَعْضُهُمْ عَلٰى بَعْضٍ يَّتَسَآءَلُوْنَ‏(27)\nWAAQBALA KHALAA A’LAA ELAA YYATASAAALOONA.\nAnd they will turn to one another, and question one another. \nقَالُوْۤا اِنَّكُمْ كُنْتُمْ تَاْتُوْنَنَا عَنِ الْيَمِيْنِ‏(28)\nQAALOO INNAKUM KUNTUM TAATOONANAA A’NIL YAMEENE.\nThey will say: “It was ye who used to come to us from the right hand (of power and authority)!” \nقَالُوْا بَلْ لَّمْ تَكُوْنُوْا مُؤْمِنِيْنَۚ‏(29)\nQAALOO BAL LAM TAKOONOO MUMENEENA.\nThey will reply: “Nay, ye yourselves had no Faith! \nوَمَا كَانَ لَنَا عَلَيْكُمْ مِّنْ سُلْطٰنِۚ بَلْ كُنْتُمْ قَوْمًا طٰغِيْنَ‏(30)\nWA MAA KAANA LANAA A’LAYKUM MIN SULTAANE BAL KUNTUM QAWMAN TAAGHEENA.\n“Nor had we any authority over you. Nay, it was ye who were a people in obstinate rebellion! \nفَحَقَّ عَلَيْنَا قَوْلُ رَبِّنَآ ۖ اِنَّا لَذَآئِقُوْنَ‏(31)\nFA HAQQA A’LAYNAA QAWLU RABBENAA INNAA LAZAAEQOONA.\n“So now has been proved true, against us, the word of our Lord that we shall indeed (have to) taste (the punishment of our sins). \nفَاَغْوَيْنٰكُمْ اِنَّا كُنَّا غٰوِيْنَ‏(32)\nFAAGHWAYNAAKUM INNAA KUNNAA GHAAWEENA.\n“We led you astray: for truly we were ourselves astray.” \nفَاِنَّهُمْ يَوْمَئِذٍ فِى الْعَذَابِ مُشْتَرِكُوْنَ‏(33)\nFA INNAHUM YAWMA-EZIN FIL A’ZAABE MUSHTAREKOONA.\nTruly, that Day, they will (all) share in the Penalty. \nاِنَّا كَذٰلِكَ نَفْعَلُ بِالْمُجْرِمِيْنَ‏(34)\nINNAA KAZAALEKA NAFA’ALU BE-MUJREMEEN.\nVerily that is how We shall deal with Sinners. \nاِنَّهُمْ كَانُوْۤا اِذَا قِيْلَ لَهُمْ لَاۤ اِلٰهَ اِلَّا اللّٰهُۙ يَسْتَكْبِرُوْنَۙ‏(35)\nINNAHUM KAANOO EZAA QEELA LAHUM LAA ELAAHA ILLAA LAAHO YASTAKBEROONA.\nFor they, when they were told that there is no god except Allah, would puff themselves up with Pride, \nوَيَقُوْلُوْنَ اَئِنَّا لَتٰرِكُوْۤا اٰلِهَتِنَا لِشَاعِرٍ مَّجْنُوْنٍ ؕ‏(36)\nWA YAQOOLOONA A-INNAA LATAAREKOOA AAALEHATENAA LESHAAE’ERIN MMAJNOONIN.\nAnd say: “What! shall we give up our gods for the sake of a Poet possessed?” \nبَلْ جَآءَ بِالْحَقِّ وَصَدَّقَ الْمُرْسَلِيْنَ‏(37)\nBAL JAAA-A BIL-HAQQE WA SADDAQA MURSALEEN.\nNay! he has come with the (very) Truth, and he confirms (the Message of) the messengers (before him). \nاِنَّكُمْ لَذَآئِقُوا الْعَذَابِ الْاَلِيْمِۚ‏(38)\nINNAKUM LAZAAEQOOA A’ZAABE AL-AALEEME.\nYe shall indeed taste of the Grievous Penalty;- \nوَمَا تُجْزَوْنَ اِلَّا مَا كُنْتُمْ تَعْمَلُوْنَۙ‏(39)\nWA MAA TUJZAWNA ILLAA MAA KUNTUM TA’MALOON.\nBut it will be no more than the retribution of (the Evil) that ye have wrought;- \nاِلَّا عِبَادَ اللّٰهِ الْمُخْلَصِيْنَ‏(40)\nILLAA E’BAADAL LAAHE AL-MUKHLASEENA.\nBut the sincere (and devoted) Servants of Allah, \nاُولٰٓئِكَ لَهُمْ رِزْقٌ مَّعْلُوْمٌۙ‏(41)\nOOLAAA-EKA LAHUM REZQUN MMAA’LOOMUN.\nFor them is a Sustenance determined, \nفَوَاكِهُۚ وَهُمْ مُّكْرَمُوْنَۙ‏(42)\nFAWAAKEHU WA HUM MMUKRAMOONA.\nFruits (Delights); and they (shall enjoy) honour and dignity, \nفِىْ جَنّٰتِ النَّعِيْمِۙ‏(43)\nFEE JANNATIN NA-E’EM.\nIn Gardens of Felicity, \nعَلٰى سُرُرٍ مُّتَقٰبِلِيْنَ‏(44)\nA’LAA SORORIM MOTAQAABELEENA.\nFacing each other on Thrones (of Dignity): \nيُطَافُ عَلَيْهِمْ بِكَاْسٍ مِّنْ مَّعِيْنٍۢ ۙ‏(45)\nYUTAAFU A’LAYHIM BE-KA’SIN MIN MA-E’ENIL.\nRound will be passed to them a Cup from a clear-flowing fountain, \nبَيْضَآءَ لَذَّةٍ لِّلشّٰرِبِيْنَ ۖۚ‏(46)\nBAYZAAA-A LAZZATIN LLELSSHAAREBEENA.\nCrystal-white, of a taste delicious to those who drink (thereof), \nلَا فِيْهَا غَوْلٌ وَّلَا هُمْ عَنْهَا يُنْزَفُوْنَ‏(47)\nLAA FEEHAA GHAWLUN WA LAA HUM A’NHAA YUNZAFOONA.\nFree from headiness; nor will they suffer intoxication therefrom. \nوَعِنْدَهُمْ قٰصِرٰتُ الطَّرْفِ عِيْنٌۙ‏(48)\nWAE’ENDAHUM QAASERAATUT TARFE E’ENUN.\nAnd besides them will be chaste women, restraining their glances, with big eyes (of wonder and beauty). \nكَاَنَّهُنَّ بَيْضٌ مَّكْنُوْنٌ‏(49)\nKA-ANNAHUNNAL BAYZUN MMAKNOONUN.\nAs if they were (delicate) eggs closely guarded. \nفَاَقْبَلَ بَعْضُهُمْ عَلٰى بَعْضٍ يَّتَسَآءَلُوْنَ‏(50)\nFAAQBALA KHALAA A’LAA ELAA YYATASAAALOONA.\nThen they will turn to one another and question one another. \nقَالَ قَآئِلٌ مِّنْهُمْ اِنِّىْ كَانَ لِىْ قَرِيْنٌۙ‏(51)\nQAALA QAAELUN MINHUM INNEE KAANA LEE QAREENUN.\nOne of them will start the talk and say: “I had an intimate companion (on the earth), \nيَقُوْلُ اَءِ نَّكَ لَمِنَ الْمُصَدِّقِيْنَ‏(52)\nYAQOOLO AAE NNAKA LAMENAS AL-MUSADDEQEENA.\n“Who used to say, 'what! art thou amongst those who bear witness to the Truth (of the Message)? \nءَاِذَا مِتْنَا وَكُنَّا تُرَابًا وَّعِظَامًا ءَاِنَّا لَمَدِيْنُوْنَ‏(53)\nA-EZAA MITNAA KUNNAA TORAABANW WA E’ZAAMAN A-INNAA LAMADEENOONA.\n“'When we die and become dust and bones, shall we indeed receive rewards and punishments?'“ \nقَالَ هَلْ اَنْتُمْ مُّطَّلِعُوْنَ‏(54)\nQAALA HAL ANTUM MMUTTALEU’OONA.\n(A voice) said: “Would ye like to look down?” \nفَاطَّلَعَ فَرَاٰهُ فِىْ سَوَآءِ الْجَحِيْمِ‏(55)\nFAATTALAA’A FA RA-AAHO FEE SAWAAA-IL JAHEEM.\nHe looked down and saw him in the midst of the Fire. \nقَالَ تَاللّٰهِ اِنْ كِدْتَّ لَتُرْدِيْنِۙ‏(56)\nQAALA TAALLLAAHE IN KEDTTA LATURDEENE.\nHe said: “By Allah! thou wast little short of bringing me to perdition! \nوَلَوْلَا نِعْمَةُ رَبِّىْ لَكُنْتُ مِنَ الْمُحْضَرِيْنَ‏(57)\nWA LAWLAA NEA’MATU RABBEE LAKUNTU MENAL MOHZAREEN.\n“Had it not been for the Grace of my Lord, I should certainly have been among those brought (there)! \nاَفَمَا نَحْنُ بِمَيِّتِيْنَۙ‏(58)\nAAFAMAA NAHNO BEMAYTEENA.\n“Is it (the case) that we shall not die, \nاِلَّا مَوْتَتَنَا الْاُوْلٰى وَمَا نَحْنُ بِمُعَذَّبِيْنَ‏(59)\nILLAA MAWTATANAA OOLAA WA MAA NAHNO BEMUA’AZZABEENA.\n“Except our first death, and that we shall not be punished?” \nاِنَّ هٰذَا لَهُوَ الْفَوْزُ الْعَظِيْمُ‏(60)\nINNAL HAAZAA LAHOWAL FAWZUL A’ZEEM.\nVerily this is the supreme achievement! \nلِمِثْلِ هٰذَا فَلْيَعْمَلِ الْعٰمِلُوْنَ‏(61)\nLEMESLE HAAZAA FALYAA’MALE AL-A’AAMELOONA.\nFor the like of this let all strive, who wish to strive. \nاَذٰ لِكَ خَيْرٌ نُّزُلًا اَمْ شَجَرَةُ الزَّقُّوْمِ‏(62)\nAAZAA LEKA KHAYRUL NNUZULAN AM SHAJARATU ZAQQOOME.\nIs that the better entertainment or the Tree of Zaqqum? \nاِنَّا جَعَلْنٰهَا فِتْنَةً لِّلظّٰلِمِيْنَ‏(63)\nINNAA JA-A’LNAAHAA FETNATAN LLELZZAALEMEENA.\nFor We have truly made it (as) a trial for the wrong-doers. \nاِنَّهَا شَجَرَةٌ تَخْرُجُ فِىْۤ اَصْلِ الْجَحِيْمِۙ‏(64)\nINNAHAA SHAJARATUN TAKHROJO FEE AASLE JAHEEM.\nFor it is a tree that springs out of the bottom of Hell-Fire: \nطَلْعُهَا كَاَنَّهٗ رُءُوْسُ الشَّيٰطِيْنِ‏(65)\nTALU’UHAA KA-ANNAHU RO-OOSO ASH-SHAYTEENE.\nThe shoots of its fruit-stalks are like the heads of devils: \nفَاِنَّهُمْ لَاٰكِلُوْنَ مِنْهَا فَمٰلِئُوْنَ مِنْهَا الْبُطُوْنَ ؕ‏(66)\nFA INNAHUM LA-AAKELOONA MINHAA FAMAA-LE-OONA MINHAA BOTOON.\nTruly they will eat thereof and fill their bellies therewith. \nثُمَّ اِنَّ لَهُمْ عَلَيْهَا لَشَوْبًا مِّنْ حَمِيْمٍۚ‏(67)\nSUMMA INNAL LAHUM A’LAYHAA LASHAWBAN MIN HAMEEMIN.\nThen on top of that they will be given a mixture made of boiling water. \nثُمَّ اِنَّ مَرْجِعَهُمْ لَا۟اِلَى الْجَحِيْمِ‏(68)\nSUMMA INNAL MARJEA’AHUM LAAAELAA JAHEEM.\nThen shall their return be to the (Blazing) Fire. \nاِنَّهُمْ اَلْفَوْا اٰبَآءَهُمْ ضَآلِّيْنَۙ‏(69)\nINNAHUM AALFAWA AA-BAAA-AHUM ZAALLEENA.\nTruly they found their fathers on the wrong Path; \nفَهُمْ عَلٰٓى اٰثٰرِهِمْ يُهْرَعُوْنَ‏(70)\nFAHUM A’LAA AAASAAREHEM YUHRAU’OONA.\nSo they (too) were rushed down on their footsteps! \nوَلَقَدْ ضَلَّ قَبْلَهُمْ اَكْثَرُ الْاَوَّلِيْنَۙ‏(71)\nWA LAQAD ZALLA QABLAHUM AAKSARU AWWALEEN.\nAnd truly before them, many of the ancients went astray;- \nوَلَقَدْ اَرْسَلْنَا فِيْهِمْ مُّنْذِرِيْنَ‏(72)\nWA LAQAD ARSALNAA FEEHIM MMUNZEREENA.\nBut We sent aforetime, among them, (messengers) to admonish them;- \nفَانْظُرْ كَيْفَ كَانَ عَاقِبَةُ الْمُنْذَرِيْنَۙ‏(73)\nFANZUR KAYFA KAANA A’AQEBATUL MUNZEREEN.\nThen see what was the end of those who were admonished (but heeded not), \nاِلَّا عِبَادَ اللّٰهِ الْمُخْلَصِيْنَ‏(74)\nILLAA E’BAADAL LAAHE AL-MUKHLASEENA.\nExcept the sincere (and devoted) Servants of Allah. \nوَلَقَدْ نَادٰٮنَا نُوْحٌ فَلَنِعْمَ الْمُجِيْبُوْنَ  ۖ‏(75)\nWA LAQAD NAADAANAA NOOHUN FALANEA’MA AL-MUJEEBOONA.\n(In the days of old), Noah cried to Us, and We are the best to hear prayer. \nوَنَجَّيْنٰهُ وَاَهْلَهٗ مِنَ الْكَرْبِ الْعَظِيْمِ  ۖ‏(76)\nWANAJJAYNAAHU AHLAHU MENAL AL-KARBE A’ZEEM.\nAnd We delivered him and his people from the Great Calamity, \nوَجَعَلْنَا ذُرِّيَّتَهٗ هُمُ الْبٰقِيْنَ  ۖ‏(77)\nWA JA-A’LNAA ZURREETAH HOMUL AL-BAAQEENA.\nAnd made his progeny to endure (on this earth); \nوَتَرَكْنَا عَلَيْهِ فِى الْاٰخِرِيْنَ  ۖ‏(78)\nWATARAKNAA A’LAYHE FIL AL-AAAKHEREENA.\nAnd We left (this blessing) for him among generations to come in later times: \nسَلٰمٌ عَلٰى نُوْحٍ فِى الْعٰلَمِيْنَ‏(79)\nSALAAMUN A’LAA NOOHIN FIL A’ALAMEEN.\n“Peace and salutation to Noah among the nations!” \nاِنَّا كَذٰلِكَ نَجْزِى الْمُحْسِنِيْنَ‏(80)\nINNAA KAZAALEKA NAJZIL MOHSENEEN.\nThus indeed do we reward those who do right. \nاِنَّهٗ مِنْ عِبَادِنَا الْمُؤْمِنِيْنَ‏(81)\nINNAHU MIN E’EBAADENAA MOAMENEEN.\nFor he was one of our believing Servants. \nثُمَّ اَغْرَقْنَا الْاٰخَرِيْنَ‏(82)\nSUMMA AAGHRAQNAA AL-AAAKHAREENA.\nThen the rest we overwhelmed in the Flood. \nوَاِنَّ مِنْ شِيْعَتِهٖ لَاِبْرٰهِيْمَۘ‏(83)\nWA INNA MIN MIN LAABRAAHEEMA.\nVerily among those who followed his Way was Abraham. \nاِذْ جَآءَ رَبَّهٗ بِقَلْبٍ سَلِيْمٍ‏(84)\nIZ JAAA-A WAL BEQALBIN SALEEMIN.\nBehold! he approached his Lord with a sound heart. \nاِذْ قَالَ لِاَبِيْهِ وَقَوْمِهٖ مَاذَا تَعْبُدُوْنَۚ‏(85)\nIZ QAALA LEAABEEHE WA QAWMEHI MAA TA’BODOONA.\nBehold! he said to his father and to his people, “What is that which ye worship? \nاَئِفْكًا اٰلِهَةً دُوْنَ اللّٰهِ تُرِيْدُوْنَؕ‏(86)\nAAEFKAN AALEHATAL DOONA LAAHE TUREEDOONA.\n“Is it a falsehood- gods other than Allah- that ye desire? \nفَمَا ظَنُّكُمْ بِرَبِّ الْعٰلَمِيْنَ‏(87)\nFAMAA ZANNUKUM BE RABBIL A’ALAMEEN.\n“Then what is your idea about the Lord of the worlds?” \nفَنَظَرَ نَظْرَةً فِى النُّجُوْمِۙ‏(88)\nFANAZARA NAZRATAN FIL NOJOOM.\nThen did he cast a glance at the Stars. \nفَقَالَ اِنِّىْ سَقِيْمٌ‏(89)\nFAQAALA INNEE SAQEEMUN.\nAnd he said, “I am indeed sick (at heart)!” \nفَتَوَلَّوْا عَنْهُ مُدْبِرِيْنَ‏(90)\nFA TAWALLAW A’NHO MUDBEREEN.\nSo they turned away from him, and departed. \nفَرَاغَ اِلٰٓى اٰلِهَتِهِمْ فَقَالَ اَلَا تَاْكُلُوْنَۚ‏(91)\nFARAAGHA ELAA AAALEHATEHEM FAQAALA ALAA TAAKULOONA.\nThen did he turn to their gods and said, “will ye not eat (of the offerings before you)?... \nمَا لَكُمْ لَا تَنْطِقُوْنَ‏(92)\nMAA LAKUM LAA TANTEQOONA.\n“What is the matter with you that ye speak not (intelligently)?” \nفَرَاغَ عَلَيْهِمْ ضَرْبًۢا بِالْيَمِيْنِ‏(93)\nFARAAGHA A’LAYHIM ZARBAN BE-YAMEENE.\nThen did he turn upon them, striking (them) with the right hand. \nفَاَقْبَلُوْۤا اِلَيْهِ يَزِفُّوْنَ‏(94)\nFAAQBALOOA ELAYHE YAZEFFOONA.\nThen came (the worshippers) with hurried steps, and faced (him). \nقَالَ اَتَعْبُدُوْنَ مَا تَنْحِتُوْنَۙ‏(95)\nQAALA AATAA’BUDOONA MAA TANHETOONA.\nHe said: “Worship ye that which ye have (yourselves) carved? \nوَاللّٰهُ خَلَقَكُمْ وَمَا تَعْمَلُوْنَ‏(96)\nWAL LAAHO KHALAQAKUM WA MAA TA’MALOON.\n“But Allah has created you and your handwork!” \nقَالُوا ابْنُوْا لَهٗ بُنْيَانًا فَاَلْقُوْهُ فِى الْجَحِيْمِ‏(97)\nQAALUD ABNOOA LAHU BUNYAANAN FAALQOOHU FIL JAHEEM.\nThey said, “Build him a furnace, and throw him into the blazing fire!” \nفَاَرَادُوْا بِهٖ كَيْدًا فَجَعَلْنٰهُمُ الْاَسْفَلِيْنَ‏(98)\nFAARAADOOA BEHI KAYDAANW FAJAA’ALNAAHUMU ASFALEEN.\n(This failing), they then sought a stratagem against him, but We made them the ones most humiliated! \nوَقَالَ اِنِّىْ ذَاهِبٌ اِلٰى رَبِّىْ سَيَهْدِيْنِ‏(99)\nWA QAALA INNEE ZAAHEBUN ELAA RABBEE SAYAHDEENE.\nHe said: “I will go to my Lord! He will surely guide me! \nرَبِّ هَبْ لِىْ مِنَ الصّٰلِحِيْنَ‏(100)\nRABBE HAB LEE MENAL SAALEHEEN.\n“O my Lord! Grant me a righteous (son)!” \nفَبَشَّرْنٰهُ بِغُلٰمٍ حَلِيْمٍ‏(101)\nFABASSHARNAAHU BEGHULAAMIN HALEEMIN.\nSo We gave him the good news of a boy ready to suffer and forbear. \nفَلَمَّا بَلَغَ مَعَهُ السَّعْىَ قَالَ يٰبُنَىَّ اِنِّىْۤ اَرٰى فِى الْمَنَامِ اَنِّىْۤ اَذْبَحُكَ فَانْظُرْ مَاذَا تَرٰىؕ قَالَ يٰۤاَبَتِ افْعَلْ مَا تُؤْمَرُ سَتَجِدُنِىْۤ اِنْ شَآءَ اللّٰهُ مِنَ الصّٰبِرِيْنَ‏(102)\nFALAMMAA BALAGHA MAA’AHU AS-SAA’AAA QAALA YAABUNAA INNEE AARAA FIL AL-MANAAME AANNEAA AAZBAHUKA FANZUR MAA TARAA QAALA YAA AFA’AL MAA TUMARU SATAJEDONEE IN SHAAA-AL LAAHO MENAL MA-A’S SAABEREEN.\nThen, when (the son) reached (the age of) (serious) work with him, he said: “O my son! I see in vision that I offer thee in sacrifice: Now see what is thy view!” (The son) said: “O my father! Do as thou art commanded: thou will find me, if Allah so wills one practising Patience and Constancy!” \nفَلَمَّاۤ اَسْلَمَا وَتَلَّهٗ لِلْجَبِيْنِۚ‏(103)\nFALAMMAA AASLAMAA WATALLAH LIL-JABEENE.\nSo when they had both submitted their wills (to Allah), and he had laid him prostrate on his forehead (for sacrifice), \nوَنَادَيْنٰهُ اَنْ يّٰۤاِبْرٰهِيْمُۙ‏(104)\nWANAADAYNAAHU AN YYAABRAAHEEMU.\nWe called out to him “O Abraham! \nقَدْ صَدَّقْتَ الرُّءْيَا  ۚ اِنَّا كَذٰلِكَ نَجْزِى الْمُحْسِنِيْنَ‏(105)\nQAD SADDAQTA RO-YAA INNAA KAZAALEKA NAJZIL MOHSENEEN.\n“Thou hast already fulfilled the vision!” - thus indeed do We reward those who do right. \nاِنَّ هٰذَا لَهُوَ الْبَلٰٓؤُا الْمُبِيْنُ‏(106)\nINNAL HAAZAA LAHOWAL AL-BALAAAUA MOBEEN.\nFor this was obviously a trial- \nوَفَدَيْنٰهُ بِذِبْحٍ عَظِيْمٍ‏(107)\nWAFADAYNAAHU BEZEBHIN A’ZEEM.\nAnd We ransomed him with a momentous sacrifice: \nوَتَرَكْنَا عَلَيْهِ فِى الْاٰخِرِيْنَۖ‏(108)\nWATARAKNAA A’LAYHE FIL AL-AAAKHEREENA.\nAnd We left (this blessing) for him among generations (to come) in later times: \nسَلٰمٌ عَلٰٓى اِبْرٰهِيْمَ‏(109)\nSALAAMUN A’LAA IBRAAHEEMA.\n“Peace and salutation to Abraham!” \nكَذٰلِكَ نَجْزِى الْمُحْسِنِيْنَ‏(110)\nKAZAALEKA NAJZIL MOHSENEEN.\nThus indeed do We reward those who do right. \nاِنَّهٗ مِنْ عِبَادِنَا الْمُؤْمِنِيْنَ‏(111)\nINNAHU MIN E’EBAADENAA MOAMENEEN.\nFor he was one of our believing Servants. \nوَبَشَّرْنٰهُ بِاِسْحٰقَ نَبِيًّا مِّنَ الصّٰلِحِيْنَ‏(112)\nWABASSHARNAAHU BE-ISHAAQA NABEEA MENAL SAALEHEEN.\nAnd We gave him the good news of Isaac - a prophet, one of the Righteous. \nوَبٰرَكْنَا عَلَيْهِ وَعَلٰٓى اِسْحٰقَؕ وَ مِنْ ذُرِّيَّتِهِمَا مُحْسِنٌ وَّظَالِمٌ لِّنَفْسِهٖ مُبِيْنٌ‏(113)\nWABAARAKNAA A’LAYHE WA A’LAA AESHAAQA WA MIN ZURREETEHEMAA MOHSENUN WWAZAALEMUN LLENAFSEH MUBEENUN.\nWe blessed him and Isaac: but of their progeny are (some) that do right, and (some) that obviously do wrong, to their own souls. \nوَلَقَدْ مَنَنَّا عَلٰى مُوْسٰى وَهٰرُوْنَۚ‏(114)\nWA LAQAD MANANNAA A’LAA MOOSAA WA AALO.\nAgain (of old) We bestowed Our favour on Moses and Aaron, \nوَنَجَّيْنٰهُمَا وَقَوْمَهُمَا مِنَ الْكَرْبِ الْعَظِيْمِۚ‏(115)\nWANAJJAYNAAHUMAA WAQAWMAHUMAA MENAL AL-KARBE A’ZEEM.\nAnd We delivered them and their people from (their) Great Calamity; \nوَنَصَرْنٰهُمْ فَكَانُوْا هُمُ الْغٰلِبِيْنَۚ‏(116)\nWANASARNAAHUM FA KAANOO HOMUL AL-GHAALEBEENA.\nAnd We helped them, so they overcame (their troubles); \nوَاٰتَيْنٰهُمَا الْكِتٰبَ الْمُسْتَبِيْنَۚ‏(117)\nWAATAYNAAHUMAA KETAABA AL-MUSTABEENA.\nAnd We gave them the Book which helps to make things clear; \nوَهَدَيْنٰهُمَا الصِّرَاطَ الْمُسْتَقِيْمَۚ‏(118)\nWAHADAYNAAHUMAA SERAATAL AL-MUSTAQEEMA.\nAnd We guided them to the Straight Way. \nوَتَرَكْنَا عَلَيْهِمَا فِى الْاٰخِرِيْنَۙ‏(119)\nWATARAKNAA FEEMAF FIL AL-AAAKHEREENA.\nAnd We left (this blessing) for them among generations (to come) in later times: \nسَلٰمٌ عَلٰى مُوْسٰى وَهٰرُوْنَ‏(120)\nSALAAMUN A’LAA MOOSAA WA AALO.\n“Peace and salutation to Moses and Aaron!” \nاِنَّا كَذٰلِكَ نَجْزِى الْمُحْسِنِيْنَ‏(121)\nINNAA KAZAALEKA NAJZIL MOHSENEEN.\nThus indeed do We reward those who do right. \nاِنَّهُمَا مِنْ عِبَادِنَا الْمُؤْمِنِيْنَ‏(122)\nAENNAHUMAA MIN E’EBAADENAA MOAMENEEN.\nFor they were two of our believing Servants. \nوَاِنَّ اِلْيَاسَ لَمِنَ الْمُرْسَلِيْنَؕ‏(123)\nWA INNA AELYAASA LAMENAS AL-MURSALEENA.\nSo also was Elias among those sent (by Us). \nاِذْ قَالَ لِقَوْمِهٖۤ اَلَا تَتَّقُوْنَ‏(124)\nIZ QAALA LEQAWMEHI ALAA TATTAQOON.\nBehold, he said to his people, “Will ye not fear (Allah)? \nاَتَدْعُوْنَ بَعْلًا وَّتَذَرُوْنَ اَحْسَنَ الْخٰلِقِيْنَۙ‏(125)\nAATADU’OONA BAA’LAN WWATAZAROONA AHSANAL AL-KHAALEQEENA.\n“Will ye call upon Baal and forsake the Best of Creators, \nاللّٰهَ رَبَّكُمْ وَرَبَّ اٰبَآئِكُمُ الْاَوَّلِيْنَ‏(126)\nLAAHA TAQUL WA LAZEE HARRAMAHAA AABAAA-EKOMUL AWWALEEN.\n“Allah, your Lord and Cherisher and the Lord and Cherisher of your fathers of old?” \nفَكَذَّبُوْهُ فَاِنَّهُمْ لَمُحْضَرُوْنَۙ‏(127)\nFA-KAZZABOOHO FA INNAHUM LAMUHZAROONA.\nBut they rejected him, and they will certainly be called up (for punishment), \nاِلَّا عِبَادَ اللّٰهِ الْمُخْلَصِيْنَ‏(128)\nILLAA E’BAADAL LAAHE AL-MUKHLASEENA.\nExcept the sincere and devoted Servants of Allah (among them). \nوَتَرَكْنَا عَلَيْهِ فِى الْاٰخِرِيْنَۙ‏(129)\nWATARAKNAA A’LAYHE FIL AL-AAAKHEREENA.\nAnd We left (this blessing) for him among generations (to come) in later times: \nسَلٰمٌ عَلٰٓى اِلْ يَاسِيْنَ‏(130)\nSALAAMUN A’LAA AEL YAASEENA.\n“Peace and salutation to such as Elias!” \nاِنَّا كَذٰلِكَ نَجْزِى الْمُحْسِنِيْنَ‏(131)\nINNAA KAZAALEKA NAJZIL MOHSENEEN.\nThus indeed do We reward those who do right. \nاِنَّهٗ مِنْ عِبَادِنَا الْمُؤْمِنِيْنَ‏(132)\nINNAHU MIN E’EBAADENAA MOAMENEEN.\nFor he was one of our believing Servants. \nوَاِنَّ لُوْطًا لَّمِنَ الْمُرْسَلِيْنَؕ‏(133)\nWA INNA LOOTAA LAMENAZ AL-MURSALEENA.\nSo also was Lut among those sent (by Us). \nاِذْ نَجَّيْنٰهُ وَاَهْلَهٗۤ اَجْمَعِيْنَۙ‏(134)\nIZ NAJJAYNAAHU AHLAHU AJMA-E’ENA.\nBehold, We delivered him and his adherents, all \nاِلَّا عَجُوْزًا فِى الْغٰبِرِيْنَ‏(135)\nILLAA A’AJOOZAN FIL GHAABEREEN.\nExcept an old woman who was among those who lagged behind: \nثُمَّ دَمَّرْنَا الْاٰخَرِيْنَ‏(136)\nSUMMA DAMMARNAA AL-AAAKHAREENA.\nThen We destroyed the rest. \nوَاِنَّكُمْ لَتَمُرُّوْنَ عَلَيْهِمْ مُّصْبِحِيْنَۙ‏(137)\nWA INNAKUM LATAMURROONA A’LAYHIM MMUSBEHEENA.\nVerily, ye pass by their (sites), by day- \nوَبِالَّيْلِؕ اَفَلَا تَعْقِلُوْنَ‏(138)\nWABEALLAYLE AFALAA TA’QELOON.\nAnd by night: will ye not understand? \nوَاِنَّ يُوْنُسَ لَمِنَ الْمُرْسَلِيْنَؕ‏(139)\nWA INNA YOONUSA LAMENAS AL-MURSALEENA.\nSo also was Jonah among those sent (by Us). \nاِذْ اَبَقَ اِلَى الْفُلْكِ الْمَشْحُوْنِۙ‏(140)\nIZ AABAQA ELAL FULKE MASH-HOON.\nWhen he ran away (like a slave from captivity) to the ship (fully) laden, \nفَسَاهَمَ فَكَانَ مِنَ الْمُدْحَضِيْنَۚ‏(141)\nFASAAHAMA FA KAANA MENAL AL-MUDHAZEENA.\nHe (agreed to) cast lots, and he was condemned: \nفَالْتَقَمَهُ الْحُوْتُ وَهُوَ مُلِيْمٌ‏(142)\nFAL TAQAMAHU AL-HOOTU WA HOWA MULEEMUN.\nThen the big Fish did swallow him, and he had done acts worthy of blame. \nفَلَوْلَاۤ اَنَّهٗ كَانَ مِنَ الْمُسَبِّحِيْنَۙ‏(143)\nFA-LAWLAA ANNAHU KAANA MENAL AL-MUSABBEHEENA.\nHad it not been that he (repented and) glorified Allah, \nلَلَبِثَ فِىْ بَطْنِهٖۤ اِلٰى يَوْمِ يُبْعَثُوْنَۚ‏(144)\nLALABESA FEE BATNEH ELAA YAWMIL YUB-A’SOON.\nHe would certainly have remained inside the Fish till the Day of Resurrection. \nفَنَبَذْنٰهُ بِالْعَرَآءِ وَهُوَ سَقِيْمٌۚ‏(145)\nFANABAZNAAHU BIL-A’ARAAE WA HOWA SAQEEMUN.\nBut We cast him forth on the naked shore in a state of sickness, \nوَاَنْۢبَتْنَا عَلَيْهِ شَجَرَةً مِّنْ يَّقْطِيْنٍۚ‏(146)\nWAANBATNAA A’LAYHE SHAJARATAN MIN YYAQTEENIN.\nAnd We caused to grow, over him, a spreading plant of the gourd kind. \nوَاَرْسَلْنٰهُ اِلٰى مِائَةِ اَلْفٍ اَوْ يَزِيْدُوْنَۚ‏(147)\nWAARSALNAAHU ELAA MEAATE AALFIN AW YAZEEDOONA.\nAnd We sent him (on a mission) to a hundred thousand (men) or more. \nفَاٰمَنُوْا فَمَتَّعْنٰهُمْ اِلٰى حِيْنٍؕ‏(148)\nFA AAMANOO FAMATTAA’NAAHUM ELAA HEENIN.\nAnd they believed; so We permitted them to enjoy (their life) for a while. \nفَاسْتَفْتِهِمْ اَلِرَبِّكَ الْبَنَاتُ وَلَهُمُ الْبَنُوْنَۙ‏(149)\nFAASTAFTEHEM AALERABBEKA AL-BANAATU WA LAHOMUL AL-BANOONA.\nNow ask them their opinion: Is it that thy Lord has (only) daughters, and they have sons? \nاَمْ خَلَقْنَا الْمَلٰٓئِكَةَ اِنَاثًا وَّهُمْ شٰهِدُوْنَ‏(150)\nAM KHALAQNAL AL-MALAAAEKATA AENAASAN WA HUM SHAAHEDOONA.\nOr that We created the angels female, and they are witnesses (thereto)? \nاَلَاۤ اِنَّهُمْ مِّنْ اِفْكِهِمْ لَيَقُوْلُوْنَۙ‏(151)\nALAA INNAHUM MIN AEFKEHEM LAYAQOOLOONA.\nIs it not that they say, from their own invention, \nوَلَدَ اللّٰهُۙ وَاِنَّهُمْ لَكٰذِبُوْنَ‏(152)\nWALADA LAAHO WA INNAHUM LA-KAAZEBOON.\n“Allah has begotten children”? but they are liars! \nاَصْطَفَى الْبَنَاتِ عَلَى الْبَنِيْنَؕ‏(153)\nAASTAFAA AL-BANAATE A’LAL AL-BANEENA.\nDid He (then) choose daughters rather than sons? \nمَا لَكُمْ كَيْفَ تَحْكُمُوْنَ‏(154)\nMAA LAKUM KAYFA TAHKUMOONA.\nWhat is the matter with you? How judge ye? \nاَفَلَا تَذَكَّرُوْنَۚ‏(155)\nAFALAA TAZAKKAROON.\nWill ye not then receive admonition? \nاَمْ لَكُمْ سُلْطٰنٌ مُّبِيْنٌۙ‏(156)\nAM LAKUM SULTAANUN MOBEEN.\nOr have ye an authority manifest? \nفَاْتُوْا بِكِتٰبِكُمْ اِنْ كُنْتُمْ صٰدِقِيْنَ‏(157)\nFAATOO BEKETAABEKUM IN KUNTUM SAADEQEEN.\nThen bring ye your Book (of authority) if ye be truthful! \nوَجَعَلُوْا بَيْنَهٗ وَبَيْنَ الْجِنَّةِ نَسَبًا ؕ وَلَقَدْ عَلِمَتِ الْجِنَّةُ اِنَّهُمْ لَمُحْضَرُوْنَۙ‏(158)\nWA JA-A’LOO BAYNAH WA BAYNA JINNATE NASABAN WA LAQAD A’ALEMATE AL-JENNATU INNAHUM LAMUHZAROONA.\nAnd they have invented a blood-relationship between Him and the Jinns: but the Jinns know (quite well) that they have indeed to appear (before his Judgment-Seat)! \nسُبْحٰنَ اللّٰهِ عَمَّا يَصِفُوْنَۙ‏(159)\nLAAHE LAAHE A’MMAA YASEFOONA.\nGlory to Allah! (He is free) from the things they ascribe (to Him)! \nاِلَّا عِبَادَ اللّٰهِ الْمُخْلَصِيْنَ‏(160)\nILLAA E’BAADAL LAAHE AL-MUKHLASEENA.\nNot (so do) the Servants of Allah, sincere and devoted. \nفَاِنَّكُمْ وَمَا تَعْبُدُوْنَۙ‏(161)\nFA INNAKUM WA MAA TA’BODOONA.\nFor, verily, neither ye nor those ye worship- \nمَاۤ اَنْتُمْ عَلَيْهِ بِفٰتِنِيْنَۙ‏(162)\nMAA ANTUM A’LAYHE BEFAATENEENA.\nCan lead (any) into temptation concerning Allah, \nاِلَّا مَنْ هُوَ صَالِ الْجَحِيْمِ‏(163)\nILLAA MAN HOWA SAALE JAHEEM.\nExcept such as are (themselves) going to the blazing Fire! \nوَمَا مِنَّاۤ اِلَّا لَهٗ مَقَامٌ مَّعْلُوْمٌۙ‏(164)\nWA MAA MINNAA ILLAA LAHU MAQAAMUN MMAA’LOOMUN.\n(Those ranged in ranks say): “Not one of us but has a place appointed; \nوَّاِنَّا لَنَحْنُ الصَّآفُّوْنَۚ‏(165)\nWWAANNAA LANAHNU AS-SAAFFOONA.\n“And we are verily ranged in ranks (for service); \nوَاِنَّا لَنَحْنُ الْمُسَبِّحُوْنَ‏(166)\nWA INNAA LANAHNU AL-MUSABBEHOONA.\n“And we are verily those who declare (Allah's) glory!” \nوَاِنْ كَانُوْا لَيَقُوْلُوْنَۙ‏(167)\nWA KAANOO LAYAQOOLOONA.\nAnd there were those who said, \nلَوْ اَنَّ عِنْدَنَا ذِكْرًا مِّنَ الْاَوَّلِيْنَۙ‏(168)\nLAW ANNAL E’ENDANAA ZIKRAA MENAL AWWALEEN.\n“If only we had had before us a Message from those of old, \nلَكُنَّا عِبَادَ اللّٰهِ الْمُخْلَصِيْنَ‏(169)\nLAKUNNAA E’BAADAL LAAHE AL-MUKHLASEENA.\n“We should certainly have been Servants of Allah, sincere (and devoted)!” \nفَكَفَرُوْا بِهٖ فَسَوْفَ يَعْلَمُوْنَ‏(170)\nFA KAFAROO BEHI FA-SAWFA YA’LAMOON.\nBut (now that the Qur'an has come), they reject it: But soon will they know! \nوَلَقَدْ سَبَقَتْ كَلِمَتُنَا لِعِبَادِنَا الْمُرْسَلِيْنَ ۖۚ‏(171)\nWA LAQAD SABAQAT KALEMATUNAA LEE’EBAADENAA MURSALEEN.\nAlready has Our Word been passed before (this) to our Servants sent (by Us), \nاِنَّهُمْ لَهُمُ الْمَنْصُوْرُوْنَ ‏(172)\nINNAHUM LAHOMUL AL-MANSOOROONA.\nThat they would certainly be assisted, \nوَاِنَّ جُنْدَنَا لَهُمُ الْغٰلِبُوْنَ‏(173)\nWA INNA JUNDANAA LAHOMUL GHAALEBOON.\nAnd that Our forces, they surely must conquer. \nفَتَوَلَّ عَنْهُمْ حَتّٰى حِيْنٍۙ‏(174)\nFA TAWALLA A’NHUM HATTAA HEEN.\nSo turn thou away from them for a little while, \nوَاَبْصِرْهُمْ فَسَوْفَ يُبْصِرُوْنَ‏(175)\nWAABSERHUM FA-SAWFA YUBSEROON.\nAnd watch them (how they fare), and they soon shall see (how thou farest)! \nاَفَبِعَذَابِنَا يَسْتَعْجِلُوْنَ‏(176)\nAAFABEA’AZAABENAA YASTAA’JELOONA.\nDo they wish (indeed) to hurry on our Punishment? \nفَاِذَا نَزَلَ بِسَاحَتِهِمْ فَسَآءَ صَبَاحُ الْمُنْذَرِيْنَ‏(177)\nFA-EZAA NAZALA BESAAHATEHEM FA-SAAA-A SABAAHU MUNZEREEN.\nBut when it descends into the open space before them, evil will be the morning for those who were warned (and heeded not)! \nوَتَوَلَّ عَنْهُمْ حَتّٰى حِيْنٍۙ‏(178)\nWA TAWALLA A’NHUM HATTAA HEEN.\nSo turn thou away from them for a little while, \nوَّاَبْصِرْ فَسَوْفَ يُبْصِرُوْنَ‏(179)\nWWAABSER FA-SAWFA YUBSEROON.\nAnd watch (how they fare) and they soon shall see (how thou farest)! \nسُبْحٰنَ رَبِّكَ رَبِّ الْعِزَّةِ عَمَّا يَصِفُوْنَۚ‏(180)\nSUBHAANA RABBEKA RABBIL I’ZZATE AMMAA YASEFOON.\nGlory to thy Lord, the Lord of Honour and Power! (He is free) from what they ascribe (to Him)! \nوَسَلٰمٌ عَلَى الْمُرْسَلِيْنَۚ‏(181)\nWA SALAAMUN A’LAL MURSALEEN. \nAnd Peace on the messengers! \nوَالْحَمْدُ لِلّٰهِ رَبِّ الْعٰلَمِيْنَ‏(182)\nWAL HAMDO LILLAAHE RABBIL A’ALAMEEN.\nAnd Praise to Allah, the Lord and Cherisher of the Worlds. ",
  "merits": "There are 182 verses in this Surah and it was revealed in Makkah. The reward for reciting this Surah is ten times the total number of Jinn and Shayateen that exist. The reciter of this Surah is protected from Shaitan and is safe from falling into disbelief and Shirk. His angels who record his deeds will testify for him on the Day of Judgement that he was from among those who believed in the Prophets of Allah (s.w.t.).\nIt is narrated from Imam Ja’far al-Sadiq (a.s.) that reciting Surah as-Saaffaat on every Friday keeps one safe from all types of calamities. His sustenance will increase and his life, wealth and children will be protected from the evil designs of Shaitan and the tyrant rulers of the time. If one dies soon after reciting this Surah, he will die the death of a martyr; he will be raised on the Day of Judgement together with the martyrs and will enter Jannah with them."
